\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{What pretraining loss and scaling results do not determine}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{scaling-law}

\p{Kaplan et al. fit empirical relations among language-model loss, parameter
count, data, and compute in \citet{secs. 3--6}{kaplan2020scaling}. Hoffmann et
al. revise the compute-optimal allocation between parameters and training
tokens in \citet{sec. 3}{hoffmann2022training}. These results concern stated
model families, datasets, and training procedures.}

\p{Neither paper identifies post-training capability with pretraining loss.
Equal loss can coexist with different probabilities for a rare successful
continuation. Models can also differ in the cost of exposing such a
continuation at inference time. Later FTIP results must therefore state which
base-model quantity enters a bound instead of treating loss as a universal
proxy.}
